<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bocas del Toro Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bocas del Toro is a province in north-western Panama on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> coast, bordering Costa Rica and including the Bocas del Toro archipelago. From the late nineteenth century it became a centre of banana growing, dominated from 1899 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-fruit-company">United Fruit Company</a>, which brought workers from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a> and other Caribbean islands. Its population includes many Ngäbe people and descendants of Afro-Caribbean migrants.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bocas-del-toro-province.jpg" alt="Bocas del Toro Province" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Panapro · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bocas2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
